{"kind":"request","text":"Builder: preserve valid upgrade status and usable recovery commands for custom home paths. Queue after #4267; retain full I7 and the earlier queue.\n\nThe original #2272 promised a machine-readable result and clear manual next commands. The current [upgrade report](scripts/upgrade.sh@b583cdc4c3bcb1f6359f3298c067ae2298b02ca7:98) inserts the home and executable directly into JSON and a shell command. An isolated run of the actual pinned script, using a valid temporary LaunchAgent, real plutil and mocked service/health boundaries, returns exit 0 with invalid JSON for a home containing a double quote or backslash. A home containing a space produces valid JSON but splits the suggested command incorrectly. The plain-path control succeeds. All four runs preserve the managed link and touch no real service or app.\n\n[Probe output](upgrade-path-probe.json), [reproducer](upgrade-path-probe.py), and [basis verification](upgrade-path-bases.json) retain the evidence. The reporting script is byte-identical to the later independently reviewed upgrade gap-closure head 854f9239501a129584dabe11d981bd214fa2faf3, incorporated in current main. This is a residual reporting condition, not grounds to discard the delivered upgrade or reopen its completed reviews. The [existing release test](scripts/release_test.go@b583cdc4c3bcb1f6359f3298c067ae2298b02ca7:350) covers rollback and pending readiness but only searches output substrings; it does not parse the complete result or verify command argument boundaries. #4129 concerns a different MCP install failure contract; #4176 remains the separate app-source upgrade delivery.\n\nKeep the correction small: encode the report as valid JSON and render the manual apps-status command so it preserves the exact selected home and executable. Preserve healthy-control versus pending-ingestion semantics, existing result fields, same-version behavior and rollback. Use existing runtime facilities where practical; avoid a new external installer dependency or a general framework. No automatic app upgrade, activation, reset, telemetry edit, tag publication or live-service operation is commissioned.\n\nExtend the existing isolated script test with a plain-path control and paths containing spaces, quotes and backslashes; parse the whole JSON and verify the command preserves its intended home and argument boundaries. Include apostrophe and shell-metacharacter handling proportionately. Test actual behavior, not a matching prose sentence. JSON encoding and shell quoting are separate requirements. Keep platform/service managers mocked and retain the rollback/pending tests.\n\nUse request/upgrade-status-paths targeting main. The cited live script artifact has ordinary staleness from a replaced test basis; I verified its actual bytes match main and cite the current test successor alongside it. The required outcome and governing authority remain unchanged, and Builder remains assigned after the existing queue. Reconcile then-current bases at intake/start. Publish exact changed paths, obtain independent exact-head Architecture/Security/Simplification review, ratify approval, seal/push source and workroom refs, verify relevant CI, and remove the owned worktree/branch. Scope is scripts/upgrade.sh and directly necessary existing tests/guidance.","body":{"branch":"request/upgrade-status-paths","conditions":"Upgrade status remains valid JSON and its manual recovery command preserves the exact home and executable for supported custom paths. Verify JSON and argument boundaries with isolated behavior tests while preserving readiness/rollback semantics. Independently review, seal, push, CI and cleanup; no live service or app operation.","head":"b583cdc4c3bcb1f6359f3298c067ae2298b02ca7","stale_bases":"git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:edd6c2fd2d0cdfb516b1acdd560f8f354660fb4f stale; retired bases: git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:235df7bfd705a08a1fdf512ecb6330c610fa1fd7